course: dictionary
lesson: 4688
title: Checking a claim with a word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «homeopathic» has two meanings. The first is about homeopathy, a kind of alternative treatment invented about 200 years ago. Homeopathic remedies are often tiny sugar pills or drops, made by mixing a substance into so much water that usually none of it is left.
explain: Read the example: «Herbal and homeopathic remedies do not have to pass the same tests as medicines.» The clue is the word remedies, which means treatments for illness, and the word tests. The sentence tells you these treatments are not checked in the same strict way as medicines.
explain: The second meaning is informal. «A homeopathic amount of chocolate» means a very, very tiny amount. Swap in your meaning: a tiny amount of chocolate still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Careful scientific tests have found that homeopathic remedies work no better than a placebo, which is a dummy pill. So when you hear a claim, ask: what is the evidence? For real illness, ask a doctor or pharmacist.
fact: Homeopathy is a kind of alternative treatment that was invented about 200 years ago.
fact: «Homeopathic» means to do with homeopathy, or, informally, very, very tiny.
fact: Homeopathic remedies are often diluted, or watered down, so much that usually none of the starting substance is left.
fact: Careful scientific tests have found that homeopathic remedies work no better than a placebo, a dummy pill.
fact: Shops sell homeopathic remedies next to real medicines, so always read the label and ask a pharmacist if you are unsure.
exercise: «Herbal and homeopathic remedies do not have to pass the same tests as medicines.» What does homeopathic describe here? | A large bar of chocolate | Tests that doctors give to children | A kind of fizzy drink | *Treatments to do with homeopathy
exercise: Sam says «a homeopathic amount of chocolate» means a huge slice. What does it really mean? | A slice made by a doctor | Chocolate with a label on it | A giant box of chocolates | *A very, very tiny amount
exercise: Which word means a dummy pill that is used in tests? | Remedy | Homeopathy | Dilute | *Placebo
test: When was homeopathy invented? | *About 200 years ago | About 20 years ago | About 20 days ago | About 2000 years ago
test: Which is the sensible thing to do if you are ill? | *Ask a doctor or pharmacist | Wait and hope the homeopathic remedy explains itself | Buy any pill and believe it works because a friend said so | Trust the label alone and skip the doctor
exam: Which is the best reason to be careful with homeopathic remedies? | They contain lots of chocolate | *Careful tests have found they work no better than a placebo | They are always dangerous to taste | They are only sold in Scotland
